---
name: ptt-close
description: "As a supervisor (designer or sub-designer), close a task reported done, reopen it, or cancel a task nobody holds. Arguments: N, reopen N, cancel N."
disable-model-invocation: true
---

# Close, reopen, or cancel a task

The command, or an AtE naming these records, approves the records this skill
writes; other work needs AtE (rules file). You must supervise the task
(`--as <name>`, your holder name); when its supervisor is vacant, the user
acts with `--as user`.

## Close (`N`)

1. Check the done report and `status.md` (`<records>/bin/ptt show <N>`)
   against each acceptance criterion and the records they cite; report.
2. All met: `<records>/bin/ptt close <N> --as <name>` (moves it to
   `tasks/done/`; a `design` task closes only when all its subtasks are
   closed or cancelled). A criterion not met: do not close; report what is
   missing and ask `1. Reopen` (the missing criteria) / `2. Wait` (the
   holder completes it) / `3. No decision, discuss further`, your
   recommendation first.
3. Carry its findings into the design (a request against the design
   document); offer the holder's session to be cleared.

## Reopen (`reopen N`)

On the user's `/ptt-close reopen N`: `<records>/bin/ptt reopen <N> --as
<name> --reason "<criterion, why>"`; the holder continues.

## Cancel (`cancel N`)

On the user's `/ptt-close cancel N`, for a task nobody holds that is no
longer wanted: `<records>/bin/ptt cancel <N> --as <name> --reason "<why>"`.
A held task is not cancelled: its holder leaves first with your approval
(`/ptt-leave approve N`), or, if gone, is freed (`/ptt-leave free N`, which
needs `--force` while it has recent records).
